  "description": "Avalonia controls that ship as types only — no styling of their own. Currently: CalendarView, a single-control calendar replacing Avalonia's five-part built-in family (inline month view with month/year/decade zoom, single or range selection with hover preview, event dots driven by the extensible CalendarEvent classes with hover tooltips, week numbers beside the month grid, keyboard navigation, and an optional picker presentation from the same control), backed by the pure-logic CalendarSelectionEngine. New in 1.2.0, moved out of the AvaloniaThemeLab default theme so any theme can use them: LightDarkPreview (one preview rendered under the light palette and a dark region side by side), Icons (a grid of every icon the active theme generates), ColorSample (one shared colour across a preview's colour controls), and the stock-control behaviours LabelPairing (a Label stacked over the field it names gets :paired), ScrollReveal (a scrolling ScrollViewer gets .scrolling), PickerPopupAlignment (a date/time picker's popup opens with its selected row over the closed box) and WheelSnap (eased snapping on the picker wheels). Appearance is deliberately left to the consuming theme: every visual detail reaches the control through pseudo-classes and templated parts, so any theme styles it exactly like a stock Avalonia control. This mirrors how first-party Avalonia controls are split — types in the framework, look owned by the theme package — which is what lets these controls be absorbed into the framework later without touching the themes that style them.",
